{
  "kind": "car_rental",
  "version": 2,
  "sum": "8b524b8d88f3",
  "about": "A car rental: cars by the day, grouped in classes that carry the price of a day; a visitor takes a class or a named car.",
  "ask": [
    "zone: the business's time zone — from its address; say it back rather than asking",
    "the classes the fleet is sold in, each with its price of a day. A letting in a class costs that price times its days, whichever rate the visitor took — the week is seven of them, and a weekly discount cannot be set beside class prices; if the client has one, it is an open question, not a number to adjust",
    "the rates' own prices (`costs`) only if some cars are in no class: those are charged the rate",
    "the cars: each one's class, and what tells it from its twins — a colour, a trim. The marks are shown to visitors beside the name when they choose a car: a plate goes there only if the client wants it printed"
  ],
